["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/Requirement", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A distinct unit representing a requirement, as used in systems, software, and hardware engineering.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibrn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Business Registration Number (IBRN)](https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/) is a unique identifier for legal entities standardized by [ISO 8000-116](https://www.iso.org/standard/75117.html). It is composed of two parts: a jurisdiction prefix and a local authoritative legal entity identifier (ALEI), separated by a colon. The prefix contains an ISO 3166 country code, an optional subdivision code, and a register code (e.g., `US-DE.BER:3031657`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/vulnerabilityExploitabilityAssessment", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A reference to a Vulnerability Exploitability eXchange (VEX) statement which provides information on whether a product is impacted by a specific vulnerability in an included package and, if affected, whether there are actions recommended to remediate. See also [NTIA VEX one-page summary](https://ntia.gov/files/ntia/publications/vex_one-page_summary.pdf).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Ned19ded3c5404dd7ac8865b9edfd3018", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/severity", "globalId", "", ""]
